  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Many metals can be used to make the anode of a X-ray tube, but only one metal is most suitable for the windows. It is beryllium because beryllium has lowest electron density outside its nucleus, and will absorb least X-ray.</p><p>Beryllium is used in making windows in X-ray tubes.</p>"
